Z||000000||wallmic||03-08-2000||08:17 PM||||Anyone have a windshield wiper schemetic?  Trying to resolve a problem as noted in my post on 3/7.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||03-08-2000||09:52 PM||||  Wallmic,<BR>    Your post was on 03-05-00. Do you think that maybe it could be you multifuction switch itself? Those damn things have all kinds of problems. Most common, I beleive, is the old turn-signal to wiper gambit. You know the one; You turn on your left blinker and you winshield wipers come on to varify your action. I would think that's the place to start. Just a thought <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||wallmic||03-09-2000||05:58 PM||||Bam Bam<P>Thanks.<P>Since my problem started with the "park" function failing (wipers start a cycle then stop)  I am first looking outside the steering column switch.<P>Any other thoughts??||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||03-11-2000||11:19 AM||||Sorry for the orientation but I was in a hurry and didn't have time to play with the scan.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wipersch1.GIF"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wipertrbl1.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wipersch2.gif"> <P>This is from my 85 Helms manual.<P>Hope it helps,<P>Carroll<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||wallmic||03-11-2000||02:00 PM||||The schemetic is great.  I also got a copy from Brian.  Thanks much.<P>The schemtics allowed me to trace the problem to the park relay (normally open contact) on the printed circuit board in the wiper motor housing.  I had cleaned it, inspected it and thought it was OK.  Turned out it was slightly out of alignment and failed to make good contact.<P>Certaintly much easier fix than disassembling the steering column to replace the switch!!<P>Again, thanks for the HELP.||||reg||7
Z||000005||wallmic||03-12-2000||09:34 AM||||Opps.  The relay that caused my problem was the delay relay, the one mounted on the pc board in the motor housing.  The park switch is operated off a cam within the motor gearbox.||||reg||4
